  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Coastal Fisheries Management and Compliance Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Pacific Islands Regional):  .This USAID activity will build capacity of Pacific Island Countries (PICs) to improve management of coastal fisheries and the effective conduct of monitoring, control, and surveillance (MCS). Specific objectives include: 1) strengthen PICs&apos; policy commitments to improve the management of coastal fisheries; 2) increase PICs&apos; capacity to organize and conduct MCS; and 3) facilitate dialogue between civil society and PICs&apos; fisheries agencies to improve collective action.  ..For example, USAID will help Vanuatu and Palau review fisheries legislation to fill policy gaps, improve the transparency of biodiversity conservation laws, and enhance the effectiveness of MCS. USAID will also support a comparative legal study on coastal fisheries MCS across PICs and help develop key training courses, including an online course on drafting legal regulations for coastal fisheries and legal training on coastal based fisheries management...This activity will contribute to the vision for an open, interconnected, resilient, and secure Indo-Pacific by strengthening natural resource governance, particularly management of coastal fisheries, and supporting maritime security. ...</narrative>
  </description>
